TypeScript is not directly supported by browsers. 
Browsers only execute JavaScript. 
TypeScript must be compiled (transpiled) into JavaScript before it can run.
TypeScript is built on top of JavaScript.

TypeScript (app.ts):
====================
let message: string = "Hello, world!";
console.log(message);

Compiles to JavaScript (app.js):
================================
let message = "Hello, world!";
console.log(message);
